<title>USA: U.S. revised Q4 GDP rose 3.9 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. revised Q4 GDP rose 3.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce seasonally adjusted GDP data on a chain-weighted basis. Following are annualized percent changes from prior quarters, in 1992 chain dollars.</p>
<p>    -			     Q4-P---Q4-A---Q3-F---1996</p>
<p> Gross Domestic Product	3.9    4.7    2.1    2.4</p>
<p> Final Sales Domest.Product  5.0    4.9    0.5    2.7</p>
<p> GDP Price Index		 1.8    1.8    2.0    2.1</p>
<p> Implicit Price Deflator     1.4    1.4    1.7    2.0</p>
<p> Consumer Spending	     3.4    3.4    0.5    2.5</p>
<p> -Durable Goods		  4.1    5.4   -2.6    5.4</p>
<p> -Nondurable Goods	     1.4    1.7    0.4    1.4</p>
<p>Pct Change,'92 chain dollars: Q4-P---Q4-A---Q3-F---1996</p>
<p> Consumer Spending-Services  4.3    3.8    1.3    2.4</p>
<p> Business Investment	   5.5    4.2   17.5    7.3</p>
<p> Housing Investment	   -0.4   -1.3   -5.2    5.4</p>
<p> Exports of Goods/Svcs	24.8   25.5   -0.9    6.5</p>
<p> Imports of Goods/Svcs	 3.8    4.7    9.3    6.4</p>
<p> Govt.Purchases/Investment  -0.4    0.7   -0.6    0.9</p>
<p> -Federal			 -4.9   -1.8   -3.5   -1.1</p>
<p> -State and Local		2.4    2.2    1.1    2.0</p>
<p>Note: Advance (A) is first estimate, Preliminary (P) is second estimate, and Final (F) is last estimate for the quarter.</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted annual rates, in blns of '92 chain dollars:</p>
<p>    -				Q4-P-----Q4-A-----Q3-F----1996</p>
<p> Gross Domestic Product   6,994.4  7,008.7  6,928.4  6,907.4</p>
<p> Final Sales Dom.Product  6,977.4  6,976.4  6,892.7  6,892.5</p>
<p> Consumer Spending	  4,733.3  4,732.3  4,693.5  4,690.9</p>
<p> -Durable Goods		 617.8    619.7    611.6    611.1</p>
<p> -NonDurable Goods	  1,447.4  1,448.2  1,442.2  1,441.7</p>
<p> -Services		    2,668.7  2,665.2  2,640.6  2,639.1</p>
<p> Business Investment	  791.8    789.4    781.4    766.8</p>
<p> Housing Investment	   277.6    276.9    277.8    277.0</p>
<p>A-Advance. P-Preliminary. F-Final.</p>
<p> Blns of '92 chain dollars:     Q4-P-----Q4-A-----Q3-F-----1996</p>
<p> Inventory Change		16.4     31.9     34.5     13.7</p>
<p> -NonFarm			  18.4     31.5     34.6     16.9</p>
<p> -Farm			     -2.4	0.1     -0.4     -3.6</p>
<p> Net Exports Goods/Svcs    -100.0   -100.7   -137.4   -114.0</p>
<p> -Exports			 862.5    863.8    816.1    825.8</p>
<p> -Imports			 962.5    964.5    953.5    939.8</p>
<p> Government Purchases     1,274.8  1,278.3  1,276.1  1,270.9</p>
<p> -Federal			 463.4    467.1    469.3    467.3</p>
<p> -State and Local	     812.4    812.1    807.7    804.5</p>
<p>A-Advance. P-Preliminary. F-Final.  </p>
<p>Wall Street economists had expected the preliminary, or first revision, of the fourth quarter GDP estimate to show a 4.1 percent increase, the price index to be up 1.8 percent and the implicit deflator to rise 1.4 percent.</p>
<p>The department said a weaker than expected buildup in inventories in the fourth quarter accounted for the downward revision in fourth quarter growth. It said that it had assumed a sharp slowdown in inventory accumulation for December, but in fact there was a selloff.</p>
<p>Commerce revised the 1996 estimate of GDP growth to a 2.4 percent increase from a 2.5 percent rise.</p>
